4px solid #b08d2e;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 18px"><strong>Short answer:</strong> To delete pages from a PDF for free, open TheEditPDF's Delete Pages tool, select your PDF, type the pages to remove (for example, 2, 5-7), and download the cleaned file. No signup is needed, and the file never leaves your browser, so private documents stay private. Your original file is untouched: the download is a new file containing only the pages you kept.</p><h2>Remove unwanted pages from a PDF</h2><p>Scanned the blank back of a page by accident? Got a cover sheet you don't need? TheEditPDF's Delete Pages tool removes exactly the pages you specify — by single page or ranges like 2, 5-7 — while everything else stays in its original order. Your file never leaves your browser, so private documents stay private.</p><h3>How to delete PDF pages</h3><ol><li>Choose your PDF file.</li><li>Type the pages to delete, for example: 2, 5-7.</li><li>Click "Delete &amp; download" to save the cleaned file.</li></ol><h3>Tips for best results</h3><p>Double-check your page numbers before deleting — page 1 is the first page of the document. The tool refuses to delete every page, so you can't accidentally empty a file. Deleted pages are gone from the output only; your original file on your device is untouched until you overwrite it yourself.</p><p class="faq-q">Can I undo a deletion?</p><p>The download is a new file, so your original stays intact. If you deleted the wrong pages, just run the tool again on the original.</p><p class="faq-q">Does deleting pages reduce file size?</p><p>Yes — removing pages removes their content, so the resulting PDF is proportionally smaller.</p><p class="faq-q">What page formats are supported?</p><p>Any standard PDF works — including scanned documents, since deletion works at the page level rather than on text content.</p>
