t:4px solid #b08d2e;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 18px"><strong>Short answer:</strong> To add page numbers to a PDF for free, open TheEditPDF's Page Numbers tool, choose your PDF, pick top center or bottom center, set the starting number, and click Number and download. A neat number is stamped on every page, all in your browser with no upload.</p><h2>Number every page of a PDF automatically</h2><p>Page numbers make long documents navigable — reports, theses, contracts, and ebooks all need them. TheEditPDF's free Page Numbers tool stamps a neat number on every page, top or bottom center, starting from any number you choose. It all happens in your browser with no upload.</p><h3>How to add page numbers</h3><ol><li>Choose your PDF file.</li><li>Pick the position: top center or bottom center.</li><li>Set the starting number (useful when numbering a section of a larger document).</li><li>Click "Number &amp; download".</li></ol><h3>Details that matter</h3><p>Numbers are drawn in a small, neutral gray typeface that stays readable without shouting. Starting at a number other than 1 is handy for multi-part documents — for example, numbering appendices from where the main body left off. Existing content is never moved or reflowed.</p><p class="faq-q">Can I skip numbering the first page?</p><p>Numbering applies to all pages. For a title page without a number, number the file, then use Delete Pages — or number a copy without the cover and merge it back.</p><p class="faq-q">Will numbers overlap my footer text?</p><p>Numbers sit 16 points from the page edge at the bottom (or 24 from the top), clear of most body text. Very full-bleed layouts should be checked after download.</p>
