der-left:4px solid #b08d2e;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 18px"><strong>Short answer:</strong> To convert a PDF to PowerPoint for free, open TheEditPDF's PDF to PowerPoint converter, choose your PDF, and click Convert to PPTX. Every page is rendered as a high-quality image and placed on its own PowerPoint slide, producing a real .pptx file. Everything runs in your browser — no upload, no account, no watermark.</p><h2>Turn PDF pages into PowerPoint slides</h2><p>Got a PDF report that needs to become a presentation? TheEditPDF's free PDF to PowerPoint converter renders every page as a high-quality image and places each one on its own PowerPoint slide, producing a real .pptx file that opens in PowerPoint, Google Slides, and Keynote. Everything runs in your browser — no upload, no account, no watermark.</p><h3>How to convert PDF to PowerPoint</h3><ol><li>Choose your PDF file.</li><li>Click "Convert to PPTX" and wait while pages render.</li><li>Download the .pptx file and open it in your presentation app.</li></ol><h3>How the slides are built</h3><p>Each page becomes a full-slide image, centered and scaled to fit a standard 10 by 7.5 inch slide while keeping its aspect ratio — so landscape and portrait pages both look right. Because slides are images, the deck looks pixel-identical to your PDF on any computer, with no font-substitution surprises. The trade-off is that text on slides isn't editable; add text boxes in PowerPoint wherever you need live captions or speaker notes.</p><p class="faq-q">Can I edit the text on the slides?</p><p>The slides contain page images, so text isn't directly editable. Overlay PowerPoint text boxes for titles, annotations, and talking points.</p><p class="faq-q">What slide size is used?</p><p>A standard 4:3-ish 10 x 7.5 inch layout, which displays correctly in PowerPoint, Google Slides, Keynote, and LibreOffice Impress.</p><p class="faq-q">How long does conversion take?</p><p>A few seconds for typical documents; very long or image-heavy PDFs take proportionally longer since each page is rendered.</p>
