id #b08d2e;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 18px"><strong>Short answer:</strong> To rotate PDF pages for free, open TheEditPDF's Rotate PDF tool, choose your PDF, pick 90 degrees clockwise, 90 degrees counter-clockwise, or 180 degrees, and click Rotate and download. Processing happens on your device — nothing is uploaded.</p><h2>Fix sideways or upside-down PDF pages</h2><p>Phone scans and mixed-source documents often arrive with pages pointing the wrong way. TheEditPDF's free Rotate PDF tool turns every page 90 degrees clockwise, 90 degrees counter-clockwise, or a full 180 degrees, then gives you a corrected file to download. Processing happens on your device — nothing is uploaded.</p><h3>How to rotate PDF pages</h3><ol><li>Choose your PDF file.</li><li>Pick the rotation: 90&deg; clockwise, 90&deg; counter-clockwise, or 180&deg;.</li><li>Click "Rotate &amp; download".</li></ol><h3>What gets rotated?</h3><p>The rotation is applied to all pages uniformly and is stored properly in the PDF, so the file opens correctly oriented in every reader — Adobe Acrobat, Preview, Chrome, and phone apps alike. Text stays selectable and searchable because pages are rotated, not converted to images.</p><p class="faq-q">Can I rotate just one page?</p><p>For per-page rotation, open the file in the PDF Editor, where each page thumbnail has its own rotate buttons.</p><p class="faq-q">Does rotation change file size?</p><p>No. Rotation only changes a page property, so the file size stays essentially the same.</p><p class="faq-q">Will rotation affect printing?</p><p>No. The corrected orientation is saved into the file, so printouts come out the right way up from any device.</p><p class="faq-q">My PDF has mixed orientations. What should I do?</p><p>If some pages are portrait and others landscape, rotate the whole file so the majority is correct, then fix the remaining pages individually in the PDF Editor's page thumbnails.</p>
