;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 18px"><strong>Short answer:</strong> To sign a PDF for free, open TheEditPDF's Sign PDF tool and choose your PDF. Create your signature by typing it, drawing it, or uploading an image of it, click on the page where the signature should go, then drag to position it. Download the signed PDF — no account, no watermark, no upload to a server.</p><h2>Sign PDFs online in seconds</h2><p>Signing a PDF should not require printing, scanning, or paying for a subscription. TheEditPDF's free Sign PDF tool opens the full PDF editor with the signature panel ready: type your name in a handwriting-style font, draw your signature with a mouse or finger, or upload a photo of your handwritten signature (white backgrounds are removed automatically). Place the signature anywhere on any page, resize it, and download the signed document — no account, no watermark, no upload to a server.</p><h3>How to sign a PDF</h3><ol><li>This page opens the PDF editor with the Sign tool selected.</li><li>Choose your PDF file.</li><li>Create your signature: type it, draw it, or upload an image of it.</li><li>Click on the page where the signature should go, then drag to position it.</li><li>Download the signed PDF, print it, or keep editing.</li></ol><h3>Are electronic signatures valid?</h3><p>Simple electronic signatures are accepted for a huge range of everyday agreements — HR forms, rental applications, school permission slips, and freelance contracts. Rules differ by country and some regulated transactions need certified digital signatures, so check your local requirements for high-stakes deals. For everything routine, a clean typed or drawn signature is normally fine.</p><p class="faq-q">Can I reuse my signature?</p><p>Yes. Your most recent signature is remembered in the editor during your session, so signing multi-page documents is quick.</p><p class="faq-q">Does signing change the rest of my document?</p><p>No. The signature is placed as an overlay on the page; all original content stays exactly as it was.</p>
