2e;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 18px"><strong>Short answer:</strong> To split a PDF for free, open TheEditPDF's Split PDF tool, choose your PDF, and click Split and download ZIP. Every page is saved as its own PDF and bundled into a single ZIP download, named in page order. It runs completely in your browser, so the document never travels over the internet.</p><h2>Split a PDF into separate files</h2><p>Need to pull one chapter out of a long report, or send each invoice in a multi-invoice PDF to a different client? TheEditPDF's free Split PDF tool saves every page of your document as its own PDF and bundles them into a single ZIP download. It runs completely in your browser, so the document never travels over the internet.</p><h3>How to split a PDF</h3><ol><li>Choose your PDF file.</li><li>Click "Split &amp; download ZIP".</li><li>Unzip the download to get one PDF per page, named in page order.</li></ol><h3>When is splitting useful?</h3><p>Splitting shines whenever pages need to go separate ways: extracting a signed page to email back, breaking a scanned batch into individual records, or isolating a single misprinted page for reprinting. Because each output keeps the original page's fonts and images, quality is identical to the source.</p><p class="faq-q">Can I split out only some pages?</p><p>This tool exports every page. To keep only selected pages, use Delete Pages to remove the ones you don't want, then download the result.</p><p class="faq-q">Are the split files smaller?</p><p>Each file contains just its own page, so individual files are much smaller than the original — handy for email attachments with size limits.</p>
